{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe Jira reconciler lives at `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/` as a separate top-level package that 47 source files load by path (`lazy_load`, `spec_from_file_location`, `sys.path.insert(engine_dir)`), with a mirrored test-side loader complex (`tests/_engine_path.py`, three `conftest.py` bridges, shadow-package fixtures). The bridge runs through a three-hop chain (`_bridge_runner` -> `rebar bridge sync` -> `python -m rebar_reconciler`), the library's `_lib_ops._bridge_run` bypasses the guarded core so an MCP `bridge_sync` runs an unlocked live pass (a bug), three retired rollback toggles (`REBAR_RECONCILER_CREATE_ROUTE`, `_WRITE_FACADE`, `_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP`) still gate code paths, five dormant modules and one dead half-module remain, `_call_with_retry` survives past ADR 0103 S3, and `bridge_state/` accumulates at the repo root with no retention. The operator approved the package move, the guarded-core bug fix, the middle-hop collapse (subprocess boundary kept), the toggle and dead-code deletions after independent confirmation, and keep-last-N retention (2026-09-06). Every finding is resolved on origin/main 083620b0 in this epic's first comment. This epic writes no ADR: the consolidated reconciler record ADR 0119 is written by the docs/ADR epic's consolidation story after this epic's package move lands, so that it cites the final `rebar.reconciler` paths.\n\nOperator sanction recorded here: the two move stories carry value-preserving key re-spells in `.github/complexity-baseline.json` (6 keys) and `.github/mechanism-baseline.json` (29 keys) with no ceiling or count change, and the toggle-deletion story runs `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --update-stale` for the removed `env_var` rows (`tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py:357-364` requires the baseline to match the live tree; precedent commit 81da792). Each such change states this sanction in its commit message.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar.reconciler` is an ordinary subpackage: no `lazy_load`, `spec_from_file_location`, or `sys.path.insert` engine loader remains under `src/` or `tests/`, and `python -m rebar.reconciler --help` works from a bare install. Checked by the repo-wide grep in the move stories and `make verify`.\n- [ ] The CLI, the library, and the MCP `bridge_sync` tool all run a live pass through one guarded core (`run_guarded_pass`) that takes the reconciler lease. Checked by the guarded-pass story's lock test over all three entry points.\n- [ ] `_bridge_runner` spawns `python -m rebar.reconciler` directly with `start_new_session=True` and reaps the process group; the `rebar bridge sync` hop is gone. Checked by the runner story's subprocess tests.\n- [ ] The three retired toggles, the five dormant modules, the dead half of `outbound_fields.py`, the two dead `MutationAction` pairs, and `_call_with_retry` are deleted with their tests; `make lint` reports `new=0` on both ratchets. Checked by grep and the ratchet output in each story.\n- [ ] Bridge scratch lives under `.rebar/bridge/` with keep-last-5 snapshots and sync logs and a 30-day alert window, pruned on every persisted pass. Checked by the retention story's tests.\n- [ ] Release notes and CHANGELOG record the package rename, the deleted env vars, and the `bridge_state/` move. Checked by the docs gates in `make verify`.\n\n## Child decomposition\n- S1 package move (`rebar.reconciler`, delete by-path loaders): criterion 1 for `src/`, part of criterion 6.\n- S2 test-side loader deletion and `tests/unit/reconciler` rename: criterion 1 for `tests/`; depends on S1.\n- S3 `run_guarded_pass` guarded core (bug fix): criterion 2; depends on S1.\n- S4 `_bridge_runner` direct spawn + process-group reap: criterion 3; depends on S3.\n- S5 delete the three retired toggles (fail-loud unconditional): criterion 4 part; depends on S2.\n- S6 delete dormant modules, dead halves, dead `MutationAction` pairs: criterion 4 part; depends on S5.\n- S7 retire `_call_with_retry`: criterion 4 part; depends on S6.\n- S8 `.rebar/bridge/` with keep-last-N retention: criterion 5; depends on S2."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788807715344319780,"uuid":"2f50f385-372a-48f2-a73a-3e9db35135cb"}